       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg per day, about double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg per day for immediate-release metformin (the absolute maximum is around 3,000 mg per day). Standard tablet strengths are 500, 850, and 1000 mg, so 1700 mg is also not a typical single dose. This may be a transcription error, and entering it as written could cause serious harm, including lactic acidosis.\n\nPlease check the intended dose with the prescribing physician before anyone enters it. If the intent was a common regimen, such as 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day) or 500 mg three times daily, I can enter that once the prescriber confirms it. Because the order involves a medication decision, it should be entered or approved by a licensed clinician."
